sentences.text:
This Court has considered the following facts while exercising discretion in favour of the applicant :-
(i) applicant is in jail since 11.07.2021;
(ii) investigation is over and the charge-sheet is filed;
R/CR.MA/23103/2022 ORDER DATED: 20/01/2023 (iii) Learned advocate Mr. Jubin Bharda appearing with learned advocate Ms. Jadeja for learned advocate Mr. Mehta has placed on record an undertaking, which is taken on record, wherein he has stated that without prejudice to the rights and contentions of the applicant and without admitting the allegations in the FIR just with a view to show the bona fide, applicant is ready and willing to pay a sum of Rs.15,00,000/- within a period of two months.

Hence, present application is allowed and the applicant is ordered to be released on successive bail in connection with the FIR being C.R.No.11201001200007 of 2020 registered with CID Crime Gandhinagar Zone Police Station, Gandhinagar on executing personal bond of Rs.10,000/- (Rupees Ten thousand only) with one surety of the like amount to the satisfaction of the learned Trial Court and subject to the conditions that he shall;
Igwosakba Promise S/O. Uzo Gud vs State Of Gujarat on 20 January, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/67928703/
2 [a] not take undue advantage of liberty or misuse liberty;
[b] not act in a manner injuries to the interest of the prosecution;
[c] surrender passport, if any, to the lower court within a week;
[d] not leave India without prior permission of the Sessions Judge concerned;
[e] furnish latest address of residence to the Investigating Officer and also to the Court at the time R/CR.MA/23103/2022 ORDER DATED: 20/01/2023 of execution of the bond and shall not change the residence without prior permission of the trial Court;
[f] mark his presence before the concerned police station in the first week of every month till the trial is over;
[g] applicant to deposit a sum of Rs.8,00,000/- within a period of 10 days from release and remaining amount Rs.7,00,000/- within a period of two months from the date of release;
[h] not leave State of Gujarat.

